  "changes": [
    "Two previously directory-only Tribal Nations receive distinct researched profiles, eight short sourced facts, four titled history layers and four direct own-site resources.",
    "Nansemond history covers river homelands, colonial displacement, family continuity and community institutions. Its environmental program is described as the publisher presents it, without promising current operation or measured outcomes.",
    "Upper Mattaponi history distinguishes the community from the 1921 adoption of its present name. Sharon Indian School construction, later replacement, closure and return are separate events. The 1677 treaty account is attributed history, not a present legal-rights ruling.",
    "Four separately reviewed directory records link two Virginia entries and two federal-source entries to these two profiles. Overlapping records do not create four Nations or establish new recognition findings.",
    "Matching Names gains an adjacent result summary, clear zero-match guidance and routes to adjust filters or search researched profiles. The original single live status remains the announcement source. Query, inventory and ready-profile mode are preserved by the results jump; all static names remain available without JavaScript.",
    "Every previous canonical record and fact clock is preserved. The targeted import adds only the reviewed new profiles and facts.",
    "Public editorial credits use ZOTHEOS and the visible game sound credit uses David Garcia. Source citations, original audio and truthful distinctions between automated evidence checks, source reviews and dated person checks remain intact.",
    "Current website cleanup does not erase earlier public repository files, commit history, copies or outside public records. No universal absence-of-assistance or exclusively human authorship claim is made."
